      "error: resolve failed for private_overlay/dag/test/claim/strategy_witness_test.dag",
      "unresolved import: module 'v2.compiler.self_host.frontier' not found",
      "unresolved import: module 'std.currency' not found",
      "name 'active_roadmap_nodes' not found in module 'gunbc.roadmap_authority'",
      "name 'accepted_roadmap_node_ids' not found in module 'gunbc.roadmap_authority'",
    ],
    reason: "FOUR CAUSES, NOT ONE, AND THE ROW USED TO NAME A FIFTH THAT DOES NOT OCCUR. The cause-lock's first real CI run reported CAUSE DRIFT here, and it was right: this row declared its cause as the symbol 'compiler_frontier_roster', which appears nowhere in the failure. What the resolver actually reports is the MODULE v2.compiler.self_host.frontier being absent, plus three unrelated breakages the quarantine had been silently absorbing - std.currency missing, and two names (active_roadmap_nodes, accepted_roadmap_node_ids) no longer exported by gunbc.roadmap_authority since they became typed refusal-carrying projections. A prose reason naming a symbol rather than the observed diagnostic is a citation that cannot be checked, which is exactly how three defects rode in behind one. The set above is the whole set, checked whole. The underlying standing is unchanged: the frontier roster was deleted at the root in public 8344, it has no successor, and public wave2_prep_design states that inventing a mapping would fabricate an authority.",
    restoration_trigger: "An operator decision on whether the private self-host claims re-ground or retract, then this witness returns ExitSuccess.",
  },
}

